---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../lib/jobs';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description={`Terms governing access to public-sector recruitment summaries and guides published on ${SITE_NAME}.`}
  canonicalPath="/terms"
>
  <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-4 text-xs text-ink-secondary">
    <ol class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
      <li><a href="/" class="hover:text-accent hover:underline">Home</a></li>
      <li aria-hidden="true">/</li>
      <li aria-current="page" class="text-ink font-medium">Terms of Use</li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <article class="max-w-3xl bg-surface border border-border-strong rounded-[3px] p-5 sm:p-7 space-y-5">
    <header class="border-b border-border pb-4 space-y-2">
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight">Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-secondary">Effective Date: 25 Nov 2026</p>
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-2.5 text-sm text-ink leading-[1.6]">
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-ink">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
      <p>
        By accessing {SITE_NAME}, you agree to use the information provided strictly for
        personal, non-commercial job search and academic reference purposes.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2.5 text-sm text-ink leading-[1.6]">
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-ink">2. Accuracy &amp; Availability</h2>
      <p>
        Although we strive to verify every deadline, qualification, and official URL
        against source notifications, recruiting bodies frequently publish extensions,
        corrigendums, or cancellations without prior notice. {SITE_NAME} provides
        content &ldquo;as is&rdquo; without warranties of uninterrupted availability or
        final legal accuracy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2.5 text-sm text-ink leading-[1.6]">
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-ink">3. External Portals</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE_NAME} links to official government websites for application submission and
        document downloads. We do not control the uptime, accessibility, or security
        practices of third-party external domains.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
